B.aFb={"Who can rush KTP?":0,"What is KTP looking for?":1,"How would I benefit from KTP?":2,"Do I have to attend all KTP Rush events?":3,"Is Open House mandatory?":4,"I have/had a scheduling conflict and cannot/could not attend a required rush event. Can I still join this semester?":5,"How many times can I rush KTP?":6,"What do KTP brothers do for fun?":7,"I can\u2019t attend all of Meet and Greet, what should I do?":8,"I forgot to RSVP for Meet and Greet, can I still go?":9,"I\u2019m a transfer student and don\u2019t have a UMich GPA yet, can I still rush?":10,"I got sick and I can\u2019t attend an event, what should I do?":11}
B.Nn=new A.bc(B.aFb,["Anyone is allowed to rush \u2014 we gladly accept (and encourage) rushees from all disciplines! In order to join KTP, the only requirements are that you must\u2026\n\n- Have 3+ semesters left on campus, not including a semester abroad or graduate program semesters\n- Have at least a 3.0 GPA\n- Not be a member of any other professional fraternity on campus\n- Attend all required rush events and submit a KTP application","KTP is made up of a diverse group of people all across campus. There\u2019s no cookie cutter \u201cideal\u201d rushee \u2014 if there were, Kappa Theta Pi wouldn\u2019t be the multi-talented, diverse, interdisciplinary organization that it is! In our experience, the qualities you\u2019re looking for are often what we\u2019d love to have in new members. In the end, we are an org united by our love for technology, and people who are truly passionate about tech are the ones who usually fit in the best.  We love (and encourage) rushees from all majors, disciplines, identities, and backgrounds.","KTP offers a supportive community of undergraduates who are all passionate about technology! Among other things, we offer mentoring in areas such as career advising, interview prep, resume development, and coursework. Additionally, we have current members and alumni working everywhere from the brightest startups to the tech giants of the corporate world. We believe that networking is far more than just professionalism \u2014 it's a process built on friendship, trust, and brotherhood.","In order to join KTP, you must attend the following rush events:\n\n- Open Rush: NONE are required, only application submission is required\n- Round 1 of Closed Rush: ONE Meet and Greet event and ONE Group Interviews session\n- Round 2 of Closed Rush: ALL events\n\nThe schedule for both rounds of Closed Rush will be released after application review.","No. Attendance at Open House is highly encouraged, but not required for rush eligibility.","If you have any questions, concerns, or scheduling conflicts, please reach out to us at ktp-board@umich.edu.","You can rush KTP as many times as you like! Many of our brothers have joined KTP after rushing multiple semesters.","Design jams, tailgates, hackathons, parties, game nights, date parties, retreats, formals, study groups, and more! The KTP social scene is very diverse and we find ways to have fun all around campus (Ask one of our brothers at Open House! Everyone will have a different answer).","We highly recommend that you attend as much of Meet and Greet as possible, but understand that you may have a conflict and not be able to attend the full amount. As long as you are able to attend at least 30 minutes, we will count your attendance. You must find our President or VP Membership and alert  them upon your arrival and departure of the event so they can help you find your group and make sure you\u2019re there for at least 30 minutes. Remember that you must be RSVP\u2019d to one of the M&G events in order to attend.","Unfortunately, due to the high volume of rushees, RSVP is required for attending Meet and Greet. We do not accept RSVPs after the deadline has passed and the form is closed. We do not make exceptions for any rushee to be as fair as possible in the rush process. Unfortunately, since Meet and Greet is mandatory for rush eligibility, not being RSVP'd to Meet and Greet implies in rush ineligibility.","Of course! Please enter a 0 in the GPA portion of your application and let us know this in the additional notes section.","If this is during Open Rush, no worries \u2013 nothing is mandatory, but make sure you submit your application by the deadline! Unfortunately, our mandatory events (anything Closed Rush) are in-person only. If you cannot attend due to symptoms, you are ineligible to rush this semester. We would love to have you back next semester!"],t.l)
